---
config:
  flowchart:
    wrappingWidth: 400
---
flowchart TB
    accTitle: How a website stays accessible and quick
    accDescr: You write the pages in docs/. MkDocs builds the website with the hook and the stylesheet of the blueprint, which underline the links in the text, give the theme the contrast of WCAG 2.2 AA, load each picture as the reader comes to it and only in its theme, play a GIF with an MP4 beside it as that video, and pin the release of Mermaid. After the build, the check docs opens every page in Chrome, in the light and the dark theme, and runs axe-core on it; each serious or critical violation shows in the summary and as an annotation at its page. Without one, the website is published.

    you(["You"])
    pages["`**docs/** and the READMEs<br>pictures · a GIF with NAME.mp4<br>a picture for each theme`"]
    build["MkDocs with the hook and<br>the stylesheet of the blueprint"]
    site["`**site/**<br>underlined links · AA contrast<br>lazy pictures · a video<br>Mermaid of a fixed release`"]
    check{"The check docs:<br>axe-core on every page<br>light and dark"}
    report(["The summary and annotations<br>with the fix of each rule"])
    published(["GitHub Pages"])

    you -- "writes" --> pages --> build --> site --> check
    check -- "a serious or<br>critical violation" --> report
    report -.-> you
    check -- "none, on main" --> published

    classDef bot fill:#526cfe2e,stroke:#526cfe,stroke-width:2px
    classDef person fill:#f59e0b2e,stroke:#f59e0b,stroke-width:2px
    classDef done fill:#16a34a2e,stroke:#16a34a,stroke-width:2px
    class build,check,report bot
    class you,pages person
    class site,published done
